(1138280, 138791, 22046, '<td valign="top">Beautiful use of light to highlight the guitar and right hand. Makes a beautiful abstract.</td>', 'Beautiful use of light to highlight the guitar and right hand. Makes a beautiful abstract.', '2005-01-29 02:54:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1138283, 138753, 27812, '<td valign="top">too much ''other'' in the pic eg grass. croppping will make this a nice pic.5</td>', 'too much ''other'' in the pic eg grass. croppping will make this a nice pic.5', '2005-01-29 02:56:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1138284, 138847, 22046, '<td valign="top">This picture is very unsettling and therefor good. It evokes emotion... a faceless man staring right at us with sightless eyes... creepy and good.</td>', 'This picture is very unsettling and therefor good. It evokes emotion... a faceless man staring right at us with sightless eyes... creepy and good.', '2005-01-29 02:57:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1138299, 137504, 30364, '<td valign="top">This is a strangely appealing image.  It could be mostly a PS filter effect rather than camera technique; I think it''s camera, but I''m not certain either way in this case.  Whatever, I''ve come back to it three times, so that''s got to be good.  7</td>', 'This is a strangely appealing image.  It could be mostly a PS filter effect rather than camera technique; I think it''s camera, but I''m not certain either way in this case.  Whatever, I''ve come back to it three times, so that''s got to be good.  7', '2005-01-29 03:19:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1138308, 138113, 30364, '<td valign="top">Very nice.  A very suitable composition for the subject chosen and especially for the challenge.  Plus an intelligent, thought-provoking title.  7</td>', 'Very nice.  A very suitable composition for the subject chosen and especially for the challenge.  Plus an intelligent, thought-provoking title.  7', '2005-01-29 03:27:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1138312, 138431, 30364, '<td valign="top">Other entries with "crowd" or street scene subjects are faceless only in the sense that the faces are too far away to see, or just happen to be turned away or obscured.  This one is different.  It has a point to it that is cleverly sympathetic to the spirit of this challenge.  It''s a visually striking image as well.  8</td>', 'Other entries with "crowd" or street scene subjects are faceless only in the sense that the faces are too far away to see, or just happen to be turned away or obscured.  This one is different.  It has a point to it that is cleverly sympathetic to the spirit of this challenge.  It''s a visually striking image as well.  8', '2005-01-29 03:41:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1138315, 138736, 30364, '<td valign="top">If all you''re going to do to satisfy this challenge is to turn the face away, it had better be done very well.  This one is executed beautifully.  I''ve rated a few higher because they incorporated an artistically sound reason for the face to be obscured, but this image makes my picks just because it is so visually and technically strong.  Especially like the presence of a glimpse of right ear.  7</td>', 'If all you''re going to do to satisfy this challenge is to turn the face away, it had better be done very well.  This one is executed beautifully.  I''ve rated a few higher because they incorporated an artistically sound reason for the face to be obscured, but this image makes my picks just because it is so visually and technically strong.  Especially like the presence of a glimpse of right ear.  7', '2005-01-29 03:50:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1138327, 138644, 30364, '<td valign="top">This is very nice.  Unlike the many entries where the face just happens to be turned away, this one has a reason, which to me makes all the difference.  Especially like the depth of field used because it makes the photo even more "on challenge".  Great title, but the image works even without it; no small achievement for this awkward challenge subject. 8<br/>P.S.  Second look ... This photo is very instructive; you don''t need a breathtaking or bizarre subject to produce a high-quality challenge entry, just a clever idea elegantly executed.  My own entry was a contrived load of rubbish.  Lesson learned!</td>', 'This is very nice.  Unlike the many entries where the face just happens to be turned away, this one has a reason, which to me makes all the difference.  Especially like the depth of field used because it makes the photo even more "on challenge".  Great title, but the image works even without it; no small achievement for this awkward challenge subject. 8P.S.  Second look ... This photo is very instructive; you don''t need a breathtaking or bizarre subject to produce a high-quality challenge entry, just a clever idea elegantly executed.  My own entry was a contrived load of rubbish.  Lesson learned!', '2005-01-29 04:05:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1138334, 137506, 30364, '<td valign="top">That''s brilliant!  A guy who sells booze AND weapons.  Such a wonderfully absurd European idea.  Alas, I''m afraid the photo only rates 5 with me, it''s an OK shot I guess, but the "faceless" element is nothing more than an accident in this scene ... I think it should have some artistic justification.  Sorry.</td>', 'That''s brilliant!  A guy who sells booze AND weapons.  Such a wonderfully absurd European idea.  Alas, I''m afraid the photo only rates 5 with me, it''s an OK shot I guess, but the "faceless" element is nothing more than an accident in this scene ... I think it should have some artistic justification.  Sorry.', '2005-01-29 04:16:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1138335, 138549, 30364, '<td valign="top">This is a very powerful image/title combination.  The composition looks at first haphazard &amp; anguished, which is of course appropriate, but in fact it is either very clever or very lucky.  Clever is my guess.  8 <br/>Second look ... it''s still strong for me.  I suppose it won''t rate all that highly in the results; it''s not a beautiful picture and will not get any of the "Oh wow, that''s sooo cool!" comments.  However, it is the most creative artistic idea anyone had in this challenge.  So bump up to 9.</td>', 'This is a very powerful image/title combination.  The composition looks at first haphazard & anguished, which is of course appropriate, but in fact it is either very clever or very lucky.  Clever is my guess.  8 Second look ... it''s still strong for me.  I suppose it won''t rate all that highly in the results; it''s not a beautiful picture and will not get any of the "Oh wow, that''s sooo cool!" comments.  However, it is the most creative artistic idea anyone had in this challenge.  So bump up to 9.', '2005-01-29 04:18:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1138336, 138684, 30364, '<td valign="top">This is very thoughtful ... a simple idea executed effectively.  Well composed, especially for the point you''re making.  7</td>', 'This is very thoughtful ... a simple idea executed effectively.  Well composed, especially for the point you''re making.  7', '2005-01-29 04:21:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1138338, 139240, 30364, '<td valign="top">Pretty good.  I think having a reason for the averted or obscured face makes all the difference, in terms of satisfying the spirit of this challenge.  Very few entries have any reason at all.  8</td>', 'Pretty good.  I think having a reason for the averted or obscured face makes all the difference, in terms of satisfying the spirit of this challenge.  Very few entries have any reason at all.  8', '2005-01-29 04:23:22.000000', NULL, 1),
