(1138420, 138537, 30364, '<td valign="top">This is a very subtle interpretation of the challenge; superficially it''s just a guy facing the other way.  But given what he''s doing, plus the title you''ve chosen, I figure you also meant "faceless" in another sense entirely.  Which lifts this simple image up the order, for me.  Nice.  7</td>', 'This is a very subtle interpretation of the challenge; superficially it''s just a guy facing the other way.  But given what he''s doing, plus the title you''ve chosen, I figure you also meant "faceless" in another sense entirely.  Which lifts this simple image up the order, for me.  Nice.  7', '2005-01-29 06:59:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1138429, 139266, 30364, '<td valign="top">I predict this will score high.  It''s a very eye-catching image; strikingly composed &amp; exploiting an arresting colour; looks good even as a thumbnail.  The ideal DPC entry.  My only minor quibble is that the facelessness is unmotivated ... it satisfies the challenge but doesn''t challenge the viewer.   7</td>', 'I predict this will score high.  It''s a very eye-catching image; strikingly composed & exploiting an arresting colour; looks good even as a thumbnail.  The ideal DPC entry.  My only minor quibble is that the facelessness is unmotivated ... it satisfies the challenge but doesn''t challenge the viewer.   7', '2005-01-29 07:12:59.000000', NULL, 1),
