(1141720, 137729, 25024, '<td valign="top">You woz robbed! Seriously I really expected this to be amongst the ribbopns I really liked everything about this shot. Never mind, better luck next time.</td>', 'You woz robbed! Seriously I really expected this to be amongst the ribbopns I really liked everything about this shot. Never mind, better luck next time.', '2005-01-31 05:41:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(1141724, 138922, 6999, '<td valign="top">Your sense of composition remains an object lesson to us all - in fact, an object lesson to any photographer I could think of. Proper photography.</td>', 'Your sense of composition remains an object lesson to us all - in fact, an object lesson to any photographer I could think of. Proper photography.', '2005-01-31 05:44:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(1141726, 138443, 17233, '<td valign="top">I absolutely love this shot and I''m soooo pleased that it ribboned. I''m a huge fan of highkey and this is beautifully composed and shot.</td>', 'I absolutely love this shot and I''m soooo pleased that it ribboned. I''m a huge fan of highkey and this is beautifully composed and shot.', '2005-01-31 05:52:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1141730, 138431, 6999, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all for votes and comments. My second 4th of the year (once described as the worst of all possible finishes). a few poeple picked up on the confusion at the top of frame, which I did want to try and do something about - but cropping to the edges of the clock faces relegated them in the composition too far, and cloning out the other people there ... well, after a while it just seemed wrong - part of the point was the press and rush and chaos of the people. The crop overall is so narrow because that''s how this scene is - immediately to the left of this we get into cafe-world, and that over-confused things, and immediately to the right there''s a line of trees, likewise.<br/> <br/>Oh - and for those who crave expensive cameras, the one used for this shot cost £110.<br/> <br/>Oh again; this was challenge number 301, it appears.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-02-02 13:32:55.</i></td>', 'Thanks to all for votes and comments. My second 4th of the year (once described as the worst of all possible finishes). a few poeple picked up on the confusion at the top of frame, which I did want to try and do something about - but cropping to the edges of the clock faces relegated them in the composition too far, and cloning out the other people there ... well, after a while it just seemed wrong - part of the point was the press and rush and chaos of the people. The crop overall is so narrow because that''s how this scene is - immediately to the left of this we get into cafe-world, and that over-confused things, and immediately to the right there''s a line of trees, likewise. Oh - and for those who crave expensive cameras, the one used for this shot cost £110. Oh again; this was challenge number 301, it appears.', '2005-01-31 05:56:14.000000', '2005-02-02 13:32:55.000000', 0),
(1141736, 138431, 14603, '<td valign="top">I like this very much and think that it works well with the busier top end..it would have been nice to have them space themselves out neatly for you..but life is seldom that kind to us.However, I feel the concept of the numbers increasing as you scan up the image really adds to it`s impact.<br/> <br/>I didn`t get round to voting in this challenge but this would have scored very highly if I had.<br/> <br/>Nice work Ed...shame about the 4th :)</td>', 'I like this very much and think that it works well with the busier top end..it would have been nice to have them space themselves out neatly for you..but life is seldom that kind to us.However, I feel the concept of the numbers increasing as you scan up the image really adds to it`s impact. I didn`t get round to voting in this challenge but this would have scored very highly if I had. Nice work Ed...shame about the 4th :)', '2005-01-31 06:13:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1141737, 139080, 14603, '<td valign="top">Well done that man !<br/>Thoroughly deserved.</td>', 'Well done that man !Thoroughly deserved.', '2005-01-31 06:16:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(1141739, 138916, 14603, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot.. and from what I`ve seen of your work so far..I think this will be the first of many.<br/>Congratulations.</td>', 'Beautiful shot.. and from what I`ve seen of your work so far..I think this will be the first of many.Congratulations.', '2005-01-31 06:17:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1141741, 138443, 14603, '<td valign="top">Very nicely done.<br/>No surprise to see this shot in a ribbon winning position.<br/>Congratulations.</td>', 'Very nicely done.No surprise to see this shot in a ribbon winning position.Congratulations.', '2005-01-31 06:21:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(1141746, 138903, 14603, '<td valign="top">A great image with lots of "atmosphere" due.. mainly, to the way you`ve handled it.<br/>This could very well have ribboned.<br/>Congratulations on your top ten finish Marj.</td>', 'A great image with lots of "atmosphere" due.. mainly, to the way you`ve handled it.This could very well have ribboned.Congratulations on your top ten finish Marj.', '2005-01-31 06:26:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(1141759, 139215, 14603, '<td valign="top">Well you certainly evoked a bit of response with this one Thamer.<br/>Very brave of you and nicely done..the graininess helps enormously to give it impact.<br/>Deserved better.</td>', 'Well you certainly evoked a bit of response with this one Thamer.Very brave of you and nicely done..the graininess helps enormously to give it impact.Deserved better.', '2005-01-31 06:41:24.000000', NULL, 0),
