(1142256, 138814, 25397, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pcody:</b></div><hr/><i> Excellent work Joey. Are you in a school for gifted students? You really should be. Or better yet, find yourself a mentor, someone you admire, in your area and become his/her assistant. That way, you can earn yourself a camera worth your artistic abilities. It should be easy to convince a smart person to take you in based on the few pictures in your portfolio here, especially the quality you produce from the camera you use.Tricking someone is one thing, but being good is quite another. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thank you for the excellent advice and compliments! Right now I work at an internet-affiliate place building their web sites but it''s pretty boring and doesn''t really let me do anything creative but make banners and sidebars in photoshop. But, I also teach art lessons to younger children. I have an exibit at the local art gallery with mostly some paintings and a few photographs. During the summer I was planning apply to the local newspaper as a photographer and also try the cable company because I love film and video more than anything and there is so much I want to learn in that field. So yep, theres my scoop... I also paint murals and some yearbook photography in my school for my community hours of service! (In Canada you need 40 to pass highschool.)</td>', 'Originally posted by pcody: Excellent work Joey. Are you in a school for gifted students? You really should be. Or better yet, find yourself a mentor, someone you admire, in your area and become his/her assistant. That way, you can earn yourself a camera worth your artistic abilities. It should be easy to convince a smart person to take you in based on the few pictures in your portfolio here, especially the quality you produce from the camera you use.Tricking someone is one thing, but being good is quite another.  Thank you for the excellent advice and compliments! Right now I work at an internet-affiliate place building their web sites but it''s pretty boring and doesn''t really let me do anything creative but make banners and sidebars in photoshop. But, I also teach art lessons to younger children. I have an exibit at the local art gallery with mostly some paintings and a few photographs. During the summer I was planning apply to the local newspaper as a photographer and also try the cable company because I love film and video more than anything and there is so much I want to learn in that field. So yep, theres my scoop... I also paint murals and some yearbook photography in my school for my community hours of service! (In Canada you need 40 to pass highschool.)', '2005-01-31 13:11:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(1142286, 138557, 19708, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bear_music:</b></div><hr/><i> Sheesh, Brad; with a title like "Rites of Manhood" what did you EXPECT?</i></td></tr></table> <br/>Still think the title is fitting. These young men go out and vie for position and ultimately are trying to prove themselves better than the other guy.<br/>Oh well, meant something to me, and that''s all that matters. Would have been happy with a Brown here.</td>', 'Originally posted by bear_music: Sheesh, Brad; with a title like "Rites of Manhood" what did you EXPECT? Still think the title is fitting. These young men go out and vie for position and ultimately are trying to prove themselves better than the other guy.Oh well, meant something to me, and that''s all that matters. Would have been happy with a Brown here.', '2005-01-31 13:23:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1142305, 138431, 1031, '<td valign="top">I caught the contrast between the clock faces and the faceless people, but to be honest, I don''t think I noticed the "extra" relevance of the person in the wheelchair -- there are so many people in chairs around where I live that they are usually treated more "normally" than in many places.<br/> <br/>I still use my 4 year-old Olympus a lot too ... nice work!</td>', 'I caught the contrast between the clock faces and the faceless people, but to be honest, I don''t think I noticed the "extra" relevance of the person in the wheelchair -- there are so many people in chairs around where I live that they are usually treated more "normally" than in many places. I still use my 4 year-old Olympus a lot too ... nice work!', '2005-01-31 13:37:26.000000', NULL, 0),
